& [VerifierContract] is independent static inspection
  + [verifier_identity] is cantor-process-verifier/0.1
  + exact digest-valid validation and compilation evidence is required but compiler success is not sufficient evidence
  + compiler IR, procedure, source-map, and cost identities are independently re-derived
  + Process IR must be the exact lowering of candidate schemas, anchors, processes, effects, and bounds
  + schema and type closure, source-map coverage, graph reachability, terminal paths, effect wall, prohibited operations, recognized anchors, lifecycle, bounds, and normalized replay are checked
  + VerificationReceipt binds exact candidate source, compiler, IR, procedure, anchor set, effect declaration, bound set, evidence, residuals, and receipt digest
  + any failed obligation returns a refused verification receipt without later authority

& [FakeObserverContract] is exact one-procedure admission
  + [observer_identity] is cantor-fake-observer/0.1
  + self-digesting policy binds exact candidate, source, compiler, verifier, IR, procedure, anchors, effects, bounds, invocation contexts, and revocation conditions
  + admission consumes exact validation, compilation, verification, IR, procedure, and policy evidence
  + stale, forged, changed, refused, blank, or over-bound inputs return refusal with no invocation context
  + successful disposition applies to one exact bounded procedure only

& [ReviewCorrections] are incorporated
  + stable identities alone are insufficient and every verifier or admission transition binds exact content digests
  + self-consistent but candidate-divergent IR is refused
  + terminal regions end in return or fault without successor and every reachable region has a terminal path
  + refused policy produces refusal diagnostics rather than admission language
  + admitted or qualified disposition requires passed validation, compilation, and verification

& [AuthoritySeparation] is explicit
  + verification is not admission and admission is not catalogue insertion or invocation
  + neither disposition proves truth, universal safety, fitness, consent, or external effect authority
  + no textual parser, catalogue mutation, interpreter, scheduler, provider, persistence, service, model execution, external effect, WASM, native backend, FPGA, or device surface is present

& [SolutionDisposition] is accepted for CPPE-I04 after completed-work review
